  "body": "## What changed (P0)\n\n#237: a ball r30 UV-meshed at 120x60 or finer, with a 10x10x100 square rod (or a 6x6x80 rod, or a 40x4x100 flat bar) through its centre, read a **trusted** X or Y axis - turning about it would sweep the rod into a disc. The ball's facets all meet at its centre, so they share a pencil with the rod's faces; their latitudes run continuously about a cross axis, one \"wide\" class that #223's per-class ring check leaves to `off_cone`, and the rod's faces hid inside it.\n\n`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis_point.rs`:\n\n- new `folded(ds, u)`: each wide latitude class is cut into `LAT_BIN` = 0.02 latitude bins; per bin, the area-weighted resultant of the 1st-4th bearing harmonics. A revolve's bin cancels them; a rod's two opposite faces keep nearly all of the 2nd harmonic, a flat bar's sides and end caps (a quarter turn apart) the 4th. A bin past `FOLD` = 0.5 counts `fold * area`.\n- `borne_out`: a pencil whose folded area passes `FOLD_SHARE` = 2 % of the inlier area does not bear the axis out. The 10 % bias budget was not enough: the 6x6x80 rod's faces are ~7 % of the inliers. The measure reads only wide classes, which a turned part's narrow rings never are.\n- Known consequence (fail closed): a square section inside a dome, judged about its true axis, is refused too (4th harmonic); a hex (6th) is not.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#237).\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, on c9a9fb3)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --tests`: 611 passed; failures only `swarf_pose_continuity` x2 (known on main) and `rotary_dflat::a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement` - **identical failure on main** (\"normals share no rotation axis\"), filed as #246.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --tests`: 1018 passed; only `drilling_axial::a_drill_where_the_model_has_no_hole_is_convicted` fails (known on main). No axis-fit refusal anywhere in the app suites.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (after the second commit).\n- All 56 `multiaxis` unit tests pass - every #208 / #223 pin stays green.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/axis_wide_tests.rs`)\n\n- `a_fine_ball_with_a_flat_rod_through_it_never_reads_a_cross_axis` - balls 120x60, 144x72, 180x90 x rods 10x10x100, 6x6x80, 40x4x100: refused or Z, never X/Y (on main: reads X, trusted).\n- `the_same_ball_and_rod_rotated_never_reads_the_rotated_cross_axis` - the 120x60 + rod tilted 0.4 rad about X (on main: reads the tilted cross axis).\n- `a_fine_ball_alone_is_still_refused`\n\nChangelog: The axis fit no longer trusts a cross axis for a finely meshed ball with a flat rod or bar through its centre\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork).\n\nFixes #237\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
